     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi everyone,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m looking for computing the acoustic dissimilarity index with the package seewave. I don&#39;t really find any infos on this on internet.</div><div>There are two functions which are called &quot;<a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffspec\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffspec&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596143000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pvQn9N8eN2GrVpdjLLSee\">diffspec</a>&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffwave\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffwave&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596143000&amp;usg=AOvVaw286ET9uWoo0uC6fZODnoAI\">diffwave</a>&quot; which looks a bit similar but do not seems to really compute the index.</div><div><br></div><div>For information, that is what the dissimilarity index looks like:</div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/seewave/attach/e86c8b54dd27d/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"\"></div><div><i>Source: <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1470160X11001361\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1470160X11001361&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596143000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3JHxH3k9Zb6S_VXnZmDYFg\"><font size=\"2\"><span>Monitoring animal diversity using acoustic indices: Implementation in a temperate woodland</span></font></a></i></div><div><br></div><div><font size=\"2\">Thank you for your help! <br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\">Jeremy</font><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sfkzHF4mDAAJ",
   "from": "Jérôme SUEUR",
   "author": "65c82d09eac308cf",
   "date": "2019-06-21T14:33:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: [seewave] Compute acoustic dissimilarity index",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:#000000\"><div>Dear Jérémy</div><div>The function diffspec() computes the dissimilarity index between two frequency spectra (denoted D[f] in the text below).</div><div><span style=\"color:#000000;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:#ffffff;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;display:inline!important;float:none\">The function diffenv() computes the dissimilarity index between two amplitude envelope (denoted D[t] in the text below).</span><div style=\"clear:both\">The function diffwave() computes the dissimilarity index as the product of of D[f] and D[t] (denoted D in the text below).</div><div style=\"clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"clear:both\">Note that there is also diffcumspec() to compute the dissimilarity index between two cumulatedfrequency spectra (denoted D[cf], see Lellouch et al 2014<a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260680408_Monitoring_temporal_change_of_bird_communities_with_dissimilarity_acoustic_indices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260680408_Monitoring_temporal_change_of_bird_communities_with_dissimilarity_acoustic_indices&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596144000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12DCjxU4gsTKM7StnP0SLD\">https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260680408_Monitoring_temporal_change_of_bird_communities_with_dissimilarity_acoustic_indices</a>).</div><div style=\"clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"clear:both\">HTH</div><div style=\"clear:both\"><br></div><div style=\"clear:both\">Jerome</div></div><div><br></div><hr><div><b>De: </b>&quot;Jérémy Martel&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jeremy....@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br><b>À: </b>&quot;seewave GROUP&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">see...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Envoyé: </b>Vendredi 21 Juin 2019 15:09:38<br><b>Objet: </b>[seewave] Compute acoustic dissimilarity index<br></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:#000000\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi everyone,</div><br><div>I&#39;m looking for computing the acoustic dissimilarity index with the package seewave. I don&#39;t really find any infos on this on internet.</div><div>There are two functions which are called &quot;<a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffspec\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffspec&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596144000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0KJQLFRXKXekQQK7ylh320\">diffspec</a>&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffwave\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/seewave/versions/2.1.3/topics/diffwave&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596144000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28jyi6xx_AoM5f3VbB78m2\">diffwave</a>&quot; which looks a bit similar but do not seems to really compute the index.</div><br><div>For information, that is what the dissimilarity index looks like:</div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/seewave/attach/c265e1c33f9b1/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"\"></div><div><i>Source: <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1470160X11001361\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1470160X11001361&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471596144000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0xKRRPt2oqv3SlPu0EE-Lb\"><font size=\"2\"><span>Monitoring animal diversity using acoustic indices: Implementation in a temperate woodland</span></font></a></i></div><br><div><font size=\"2\">Thank you for your help! <br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\">Jeremy</font><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></div></div>"
    ],
